owever, with three clubs on board, I need to protect against flush draws. A modest bet of 200 chips (about 1% of my stack) will serve multiple purposes: fold out weak hands and draws, extract value from weaker pairs, and gather information about opponent's hand strength before the river card. This bet is small enough to minimize risk but large enough to apply pressure.\n\nAnswer: 200"}
